From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:43:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Inflow and outflow at each section, with their temperature
 and salinity: is a heat or freshwater error in the water or in the flow?

transports.jl: inflow_outflow splits a section's transport by direction
(same faces, areas and tracer averaging as section_transports) and returns
the inflow and outflow (Sv) with their transport-weighted temperature and
salinity. analysis/transports.jl (offline, model) and
analysis/glorys_transports.jl (GLORYS) save these under "inflow_outflow".

analysis/water_masses.jl compares them, model against GLORYS, as monthly
means, and splits the model - GLORYS heat and freshwater transport
differences into a property part (GLORYS's flow carrying the model's T or S),
a volume part (the model's extra or missing flow carrying GLORYS's water)
and the rest. Tables in output_dir/water_masses.md, daily series in
figure_dir/water_masses.png.

